    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X5eWJrnGAc1N2tw34GW6Rr)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #517); independent of the other open PRs.\n- Only adds a new package and one line in `stow-migration/packages.tsv`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New Stow package `devonthink-pdf-grey` (macOS only) with `~/.local/bin/dt-pdf-grey` (bash).\n- `dt-pdf-grey 0.3` or a preset (`charcoal`, `dark`, `mid`, `light`) writes `PDFBackground` in `com.devon-technologies.think` as a grey.\n- `--reset` restores the values saved before the first change; `--show` prints current and saved values.\n- Refuses while DEVONthink is running; `--quit` quits it first, `--relaunch` reopens it, `--dry-run` prints the `defaults` commands only.\n- `--disable-pdf-dark-mode` also writes `DisablePDFDarkMode=true`.\n- `README.org` documents usage and safety as bullet lists.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## What is not verified\n\n- I could not run DEVONthink or macOS: the script was only tested on Linux with stubbed `defaults`, `plutil` and `pgrep` (refusal while running, bad level, save-once original, reset, dry run).\n- Unknown whether `PDFBackground` is the dark-mode colour, the light one, or both. No `PDFBackgroundDark` key was seen (`FormViewBackgroundDark` exists for forms).\n- Unknown whether `DisablePDFDarkMode` is needed alongside; try the grey alone first.\n- The README has a before/after `defaults read` diff recipe to confirm which key the GUI changes.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles && git switch 520-devonthink-pdf-grey && stow devonthink-pdf-grey`; `dt-pdf-grey --help` prints usage (untested by Claude)\n- [x] `dt-pdf-grey --show` with DEVONthink open: prints the 0.4246... grey and \"No saved original yet\" (untested by Claude)\n- [x] `dt-pdf-grey 0.2 --dry-run` with DEVONthink open: refuses; `--quit --dry-run` prints the commands and changes nothing (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Quit DEVONthink, `dt-pdf-grey 0.2 --relaunch`: DEVONthink reopens, a PDF in dark mode shows a darker grey; `--show` lists the saved original (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Run `dt-pdf-grey 0.5` again: the saved original is unchanged (untested by Claude)\n- [x] Edge case: `dt-pdf-grey 1.5` and `dt-pdf-grey abc` are rejected with a message (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Only if the grey is inverted or ignored: `dt-pdf-grey 0.2 --quit --relaunch --disable-pdf-dark-mode`, see whether it helps (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `dt-pdf-grey --reset --quit --relaunch`: `defaults read com.devon-technologies.think PDFBackground` matches the original and the PDF looks as before (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Regression: `dt-open-install` and the Hammerspoon highlight keys still work (untested by Claude)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Run `dt-pdf-grey --reset --quit --relaunch` first so DEVONthink's preferences are back to the original.\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Unlink the package if you do not want it: `cd ~/dotfiles && stow -D devonthink-pdf-grey`.\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 520-devonthink-pdf-grey`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- The saved original lives in `~/.local/state/dt-pdf-grey/original` until `--reset` removes it.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB7PrmHwprV4jysmZn)_",
